# Local code first + fresh clones

All six platforms are cloned under `platform/*/` (~63 git repos). **Read and search code locally** — not via `gitlab_get_repository_file`.

## Before code work (every session / task)

1. **Sync** affected platform(s) before Read/Grep/edit on `platform/`:
   ```bash
   ./scripts/sync-platform-repos.sh              # all platforms
   ./scripts/sync-platform-repos.sh ensi         # one platform
   ./scripts/sync-platform-repos.sh starfish24/core/Order   # one repo
   ```
2. If sync fails (dirty tree, merge conflict) — **stop and report**; do not silently use stale code or switch to GitLab as workaround.
3. After sync, use local tools: `Read`, `Grep`, `SemanticSearch`, `Glob` on `platform/`.

ENSI only: run commands inside containers via `elc -w gj -c <svc> exec …` — still use **local** source under `platform/ensi/`.

## Local vs GitLab MCP

| Need | Tool |
|------|------|
| Read/search/implement in cloned code | Local `platform/` (after sync) |
| MRs, pipelines, job logs, approvals | `gitlab_*` MCP |
| Jira, Confluence, prod logs, k8s | Buddy MCP (non-GitLab tools) |
| Repo **not** present under `platform/` | `gitlab_get_repository_file` / clone first |
| Compare with remote branch without checkout | GitLab MCP (exception) |

## Anti-patterns

- `gitlab_get_repository_file` when `platform/<system>/…` exists locally
- Starting code investigation without sync/pull
- `gitlab_*` for “find where X is defined” in a cloned service
- Assuming `platform/site/` or `platform/starfish24/` is empty — they are populated

Details: `@.claude/skills/gj-multirepo-navigation/SKILL.md`, sync script `@scripts/sync-platform-repos.sh`.
